#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142622 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ef8389c-2909-5e02-a185-817ae3c6219b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "294b83f4-2e38-5bf4-a521-01fe8ca13fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-13831" :question/problem "What is the missing number in the following equality?\n\n![](images/80/805043dc7270f411d6abb0edde2d24c79b9a700fddbab6f057cf010f688d528a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we write ![](images/f3/f30ed07403432a8c183dd7a486efc7de50b792f92290af3fb54c70190f755da0.svg) as an improper fraction:\n\n![](images/ea/ea2c8853ff746445bea369a9ed84d0e70bac867b06e5a8654b0cb916bdf87da8.svg)\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n![](images/f2/f23b3a3dbbadfad8feda12f14cbadf615b49835464b98684b931c6aee5416ec3.svg)\n\nTherefore, the missing number is ![](images/e0/e008b7f9fc7f00e35668031c5cdc99067adc66c79ce950e5e4afb35f7cb9644d.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142624 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8e94ce-081f-5ea4-ac09-de30a890f4af" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Mixed Number by a Fraction When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "a688fc95-6831-57c6-9fee-f3295412af05" :question/math-academy-id "e-13835" :question/problem "Find the value of $\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times 2 \\, \\dfrac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2 \\,\\dfrac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2 \\,\\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{(2 \\times 2) + 1}{2} = \\dfrac{5}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times \\dfrac{5}{2} =  \\dfrac{1 \\times 5}{3 \\times 2} = \\dfrac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times 2 \\, \\dfrac{1}{2} = \\dfrac{5}{6}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142626 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15c48f93-e112-5d71-bb8a-c23e022931f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/id #uuid "689fd963-ba93-5b0a-b7e4-0b8fd1dc9101" :question/math-academy-id "e-13839" :question/problem "Determine the missing number in the following equality.\n\n![](images/7a/7aee3025661cf0e0b7fdf5699d8a05dbbd6a2a9a6f8040d6835cc2ec7543a1d7.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we write ![](images/e5/e5aaba9db7118349d6239ec5528b38f96038715ceb4d857bafb24cbdf7752f37.svg) as an improper fraction:\n\n![](images/46/46ebc0b6db840b22d324d6a247052efd4da7aa43778418287b905bef47bf001a.svg)\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n![](images/1f/1ff2d2bddeb4958b37e00d1808cb639dbe1d0fb321ec615880a2ac669d65c02a.svg)\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n![](images/f7/f7a7753e17912b5638bdfcfdac2706a0c8e4f49a9be350b705a1d31a3fba4403.svg)\n\nHence, the missing number is ![](images/e0/e008b7f9fc7f00e35668031c5cdc99067adc66c79ce950e5e4afb35f7cb9644d.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142627 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f0bba3-2b88-5e77-9359-b238179c7f3d" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Mixed Number by a Fraction When the Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/id #uuid "db3701cf-af70-508a-a158-5e38ff68246f" :question/math-academy-id "e-13843" :question/problem "Multiply $1 \\, \\dfrac{7}{8} \\times \\dfrac{2}{3} .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1 \\,\\dfrac{7}{8}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1 \\,\\dfrac{7}{8} = \\dfrac{(1 \\times 8) + 7}{8} = \\dfrac{15}{8}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{8}\\times \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this product by swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{8}\\times \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{15}{3}\\times \\frac{2}{8} \\\\  & =5\\times \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5}{4} = 1 \\, \\textrm{R} 1 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ef8389c-2909-5e02-a185-817ae3c6219b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36778b32-fe2e-5a0b-9886-b04c899b74d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433517} {:answer/id #uuid "5870bad9-e358-5a6c-8a43-db9fcb888d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433521} {:answer/id #uuid "7c129849-472f-5087-bb0d-c68a2fcd7640" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433531} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f06d1d-5860-5bee-a7d6-9a03b53582c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433538} {:answer/id #uuid "e12d60f0-16f1-576d-b568-1f694dccb3c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5870bad9-e358-5a6c-8a43-db9fcb888d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433521} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a1c80be-a2ff-5fbc-9875-019c9b1f98a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e8e173c2-e3a0-5762-b927-282dfe1684fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-137038" :question/problem "What is the missing number in the following equality?\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times 2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{15}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(2\\times 5)+3}{5}=\\frac{13}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{13}{5}=\\frac{1\\times 13}{3\\times 5}=\\frac{13}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $13.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8e94ce-081f-5ea4-ac09-de30a890f4af" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Mixed Number by a Fraction When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194fb4ac-3902-5a77-ba6d-33b22e986dde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433514} {:answer/id #uuid "29a3daef-b189-5536-a7bb-3ff10f853e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433516} {:answer/id #uuid "67af0e0e-1096-5530-967c-5689ac3bb6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433523} {:answer/id #uuid "68e12f3b-ff9b-5dee-a1f1-098ae1a1430c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433525} {:answer/id #uuid "f338af53-6e27-5f24-b51f-91367e3cc26f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67af0e0e-1096-5530-967c-5689ac3bb6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433523} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e0f1066-2f17-5bc8-b034-66e898b78421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea53764e-761e-56a8-95fe-208e14866e88" :question/math-academy-id "q-137045" :question/problem "$\\frac{5}{8}\\times 1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{2}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{(1\\times 2)+1}{2}=\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{8}\\times \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{5\\times 3}{8\\times 2}=\\frac{15}{16}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15c48f93-e112-5d71-bb8a-c23e022931f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05790a09-e33c-5201-a476-6666e84450e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433510} {:answer/id #uuid "3c79a6a0-cef7-5e6f-a2e6-256ebbfe016d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433518} {:answer/id #uuid "94938069-875b-5c90-ba8b-9192aceb9e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433535} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4210f6-17e4-5fcf-9b76-7def8cf793f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433539} {:answer/id #uuid "abf8570f-5794-