=1\\,\\frac{5}{7}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142804 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9f0bba3-2b88-5e77-9359-b238179c7f3d" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Mixed Number by a Fraction When the Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f260b7a-6064-527f-85e6-fcba901c621c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433515} {:answer/id #uuid "40e485e8-42ce-549d-b184-39b83341c80f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433519} {:answer/id #uuid "68ae60d3-8457-5131-9926-083a63502892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{4}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433524} {:answer/id #uuid "992bb123-cc88-514a-9006-62f7c171d850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433536} {:answer/id #uuid "e191e9e1-195d-5bb4-a6c7-9a7627f647a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f260b7a-6064-527f-85e6-fcba901c621c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\,\\frac{1}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433515} :answer-field/id #uuid "d60a1599-e1a9-5aaf-88bf-566e598dbe64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5fb302d8-e54d-5bd0-98ff-6702cdefa4b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-137104" :question/problem "$1\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+3}{5}=\\frac{8}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{5}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{8\\times 2}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{16}{15}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{15}=1\\,\\text{R}1=1\\,\\frac{1}{15}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb8e94ce-081f-5ea4-ac09-de30a890f4af" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Mixed Number by a Fraction When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8f4b43-e164-5d96-9f1d-5642c2cb95c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c8f4b43-e164-5d96-9f1d-5642c2cb95c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433511} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2cbd817-486a-5620-a720-179f9c63b8d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433549}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0a94de2-ad1f-55ec-8c96-c8bb2bd3533f" :question/math-academy-id "q-198150" :question/problem "Expressed as a fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{2}{7}\\times 3\\,\\frac{1}{3}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we write $3\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{(3\\times 3)+1}{3}=\\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{7}\\times \\frac{10}{3}=\\frac{2\\times 10}{7\\times 3}=\\frac{20}{21}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "15c48f93-e112-5d71-bb8a-c23e022931f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Mixed Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1233d239-8d6d-5dea-8e13-339cff144673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433512} {:answer/id #uuid "7a755fd8-1a57-589c-bfe9-90946db6a98f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433529} {:answer/id #uuid "7e515a28-0e68-5a29-ab6f-4c8963d1bfa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433532} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce1ef14-4b0c-5764-835c-9908acca20ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433534} {:answer/id #uuid "a2606e64-d7d7-5757-b82b-d15df09e2fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2606e64-d7d7-5757-b82b-d15df09e2fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433537} :answer-field/id #uuid "77bb0688-589c-5170-8f41-838eaf3b2029" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7104d34b-6e4e-5044-bbe9-614ca52dfdce" :question/math-academy-id "q-57114" :question/problem "Determine the missing number in the following equality.\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\times \\frac{6}{7}=1\\,\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{35}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+1}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{5}\\times \\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{6\\times 6}{5\\times 7}=\\frac{36}{35}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{36}{35}=1\\,\\text{R}1=1\\,\\frac{1}{35}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142801 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ef8389c-2909-5e02-a185-817ae3c6219b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Numerator When the Result Is a Proper Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d03689a-97ec-5895-89b2-b0cf47d52c5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433522} {:answer/id #uuid "68fd1b93-6a12-5a0d-ad65-30a74681c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433526} {:answer/id #uuid "6a78c868-1cf9-55ce-945c-76f6e81bf2c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433527} {:answer/id #uuid "74e60be8-0736-5056-b199-d66ea637defa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433528} {:answer/id #uuid "856bc86b-5ecc-52ee-8052-191e0862f1c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68fd1b93-6a12-5a0d-ad65-30a74681c145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433526} :answer-field/id #uuid "fed07750-bf84-547d-b2e9-73e2268c1c